FFmpeg Pan Left & Pan Right with Zoom using Python

Here are both effects built the same way as the zoom-out script — using zoompan with centered, controlled motion.

🧠 Core Concepts Before the Code

The zoompan filter controls three things per frame:
z** — zoom level
x** — horizontal pan position
y** — vertical pan position (kept centered)

For a pan, you hold a fixed zoom and move x linearly across the frame. The key formula for safe panning bounds is:
max_x = iw - (iw/zoom)   ← rightmost safe x position
At zoom 1.0, max_x = 0 (no room to pan), so you must zoom in slightly (e.g., 1.2x–1.5x) to have pixel space to pan across.

✅ Pan Right (Left → Right) with Zoom

Starts panned to the left edge, moves to the right edge over the duration.

import subprocess

def pan_right_zoom(
    input_image: str,
    output_video: str,
    zoom: float = 1.3,          # Must be > 1.0 to have room to pan
    duration_sec: int = 4,
    fps: int = 25,
    width: int = 1920,
    height: int = 1080,
):
    total_frames = duration_sec * fps

x moves from 0 (left) to max safe x (right)
max x = iw - (iw/zoom)
    x_expr = f"(iw-(iw/zoom))*(on/{total_frames})"

y stays vertically centered throughout
    y_expr = f"ih/2-(ih/zoom/2)"

    zoompan_filter = (
        f"zoompan="
        f"z='{zoom}':"
        f"x='{x_expr}':"
        f"y='{y_expr}':"
        f"d={total_frames}:"
        f"s={width}x{height}:"
        f"fps={fps}"
    )

    command = [
        "ffmpeg",
        "-loop", "1",
        "-i", input_image,
        "-vf", zoompan_filter,
        "-c:v", "libx264",
        "-crf", "18",
        "-preset", "slow",
        "-pix_fmt", "yuv420p",
        "-t", str(duration_sec),
        "-y",
        output_video,
    ]

    print("Running FFmpeg Pan-Right command:")
    print(" ".join(command))

    result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True)

    if result.returncode != 0:
        print("FFmpeg Error:\n", result.stderr)
        raise RuntimeError("FFmpeg failed.")
    else:
        print(f"✅ Pan Right saved to: {output_video}")

--- Usage ---
pan_right_zoom(
    input_image="input.jpg",
    output_video="pan_right.mp4",
    zoom=1.3,
    duration_sec=4,
    fps=25,
    width=1920,
    height=1080,
)

✅ Pan Left (Right → Left) with Zoom

Starts panned to the right edge, moves to the left edge — simply the reverse of the x expression.

